  "name": "Easy Strength",
  "origin": "Dan John",
  "source": {
    "url": "https://www.t-nation.com/training/easy-strength-questions-and-answers/",
    "note": "Structure only: five basic movement patterns, 10 reps a day per lift, weight held easy for 40 days. Written in our own words from the cited article, no text reproduced. A training method is not copyrightable expression (17 U.S.C. 102(b), research/16 'The licence rule')."
  },
  "progression_unit": "session",
  "dose": "sets",
  "days": 3,
  "notes": "40-day cycle. All five lifts are trained every session, always to 10 total reps, at a weight easy enough to leave several reps in the tank; the daily rep scheme is what varies, not the load. Three day-types (2x5, 5-3-2, 6x1) rotate and repeat for the full 40 sessions rather than the file listing 40 nodes, matching the GZCLP precedent of a rotation shorter than the source's day count. Every block advances on `advance_when: {\"kind\": \"user_says_easy\"}`: the coach asks whether the weight felt easy, and only a block carrying this kind gets asked. A yes adds one rep next session (`axis: reps`); a no holds. Load itself stays a human call, same as the source intends.",
  "rotation": [
